president trump's term in office was  marked by record-breaking staff turnover  including four chiefs of staff but one  constant in the west wing was kellyanne  conway she was the first woman to run a  winning presidential campaign and then  served as senior counselor to the  president for nearly his entire term she  was one of the most visible symbols of  the trump years as well and she's the  author of a new book it's called here's  the deal a memoir it's published by an  imprint of simon schuster which is a  division of cbs's parent company  paramount global and kellyanne joins us  now thank you very much for being here  my pleasure i really enjoyed the book uh  you have a lot to say uh someone said  that it's got more score settling than a  quentin tarantino movie and i think  that's true you take some whacks at  people uh which is different from how  you left the white house you said more  mama less drama  now you're back in the spotlight what  are you trying to accomplish here well  this is my memoir and  i people always ask me what's the story  behind the stories where did you come  from did you go up in a political  household  what do you see as the future for the 74  million trump voters who weren't at the  capitol on january 6 for example and i  wanted to go behind the scenes a little  bit but not with one of these tell all  and bore most i'm not speaking up now  because i didn't speak up then god knows  i spoke up then pretty much daily and  but i also i think that many women will  will relate to this book because  in most workplaces women sometimes feel  shoved to the side they feel  marginalized maybe by some of the other  women but especially some of the men  they work with and that happened to me  really early on tony i i was trying to  get my footing it was a rough first  couple of months and i think my big  decision at that time was do i slink  away and just go back home and say this  wasn't for me or do i realize hold my  head high with some dignity grace in  class try to get my footing work on  issues on my portfolio that are within  my wheelhouse and the whole time i had  the president's support which meant a  great deal because he was the guy on the  ballot he's the guy in charge and i'm  accustomed to working at a volume and  velocity that is very trump he's the guy  in charge you mentioned speaking up  while you're in office i have to ask you  about a story in the book in which you  describe yourself as maybe the first  person in the president's inner circle  to tell him he lost in 2020. the  president took to truth social his  social media platform and says that's  not true didn't happen otherwise he  would have locked you out we've got the  whole long  non-tweet alternative tweet there um  what do you say to the president uh  contesting your version no what exactly  he said he wouldn't have dealt with you  any longer she would have been wrong and  you could go back with your crazy  husband yes she didn't just say you know  no she's not telling the truth so the  that excerpt in the book really speaks  to the president coming up short before  the december 14th certification by the  electors and i had talked to the  president several many times between the  elect election day and december 14th and  saying you have every right to deal with  al gore did what others have done which  is if you're going to go find evidence  of malfeasance the shenanigans a  theft for all you have every right to do  that with your legal team and present it  and we all know what happened they they  tried they presented it the election was  certified for  biden harris but other people had  another idea to blow past december 14th  and look at january 6 as another  alternative way and i think look it's  very simple for me i've always had a  great relationship with president trump  and i go on and on in the book of how  protective he was of me my family he was  a great girl boss we have five you know  high ranking women with 19 kids highest  ranking we had 19 kids 12 daughters  seven sons ages two to 16 at this moment  when i'm looking up at a meeting at 8 20  in the morning we're all there but i  wanted to say this  that if president trump wants to be  president again it's a very simple path  he should just run against joe biden but  kellyanne i do want to ask because  you're painting a very rosy picture also  we walked away from the key question  here because did you tell the president  that he failed on november 3rd because  he says he didn't i told him that they  did not that with december 14th coming  up it didn't look like they had produced  the evidence needed to stop the  certification of the election which had  happened now there's another day that  you certify january 6th and in fairness  there are democrats in congress as we  sit here who have never voted to certify  a republican presidential election in  this century they didn't do it anymore  we're talking about your memoir and the  stories in your book yes and i did i did  and it broke my heart i wish you were  still the president because what's  happening i do yes i do i do gail  because um i think this man-made  disaster of biden harris has hurt a lot  of people we have infants looking for  baby formula we have five dollar gas  prices okay but let's just focus on  trump for a second and while you were  there because you say you can hold your  head high did you always feel that way  because i think the the consensus about  kellyanne conway was you're very good at  your job no question but you seem to  have to do a lot of spinning for a  president who was very fluid with the  truth and i i think that's putting it  very diplomatically you have former  administration officials john kelly  general mattis general barr  who say trump is  unqualified unfit for office and even  detached from reality  how does that square with what you see  as somebody who is if he wants to run  again he should well i served with each  of those men and i respect them for  their public service but they're saying  it now they didn't say it then john  kelly is the longest serving chief of  staff to president trump that's just a  fact what's your point about that well  my point is also what i saw in president  trump is somebody who was the wish  fulfillment of voters what they told  pollsters like me for decades i want  somebody with a ton of experience who's  not connected to washington who's not a  politician thinking well who's that and  here he came pre-verified as a tv star  with the number one show  obviously a successful businessman and  job creator what i think was less  charming gail is that some of the people  around him had no washington experience  i think it was determinative that donald  trump didn't have any i think that's  been killing this that's the thing okay  that's what they're saying but even your  own husband this is i think fascinates  so many people your own husband seemed  to have turned on his mind  changed his mind are totally turned i  mean you're right in the book of the man  you thought had your back ended up  stabbing you in the back you're in the  white house you're the white house  senior adviser and your own husband is  saying very disparaging things isn't  that unfortunate isn't that very sad  because george does not for you i think  that's very unfortunate thank you very  much gail i really appreciate it again i  think women can relate to that but this  was next level and i'll say this george  conway's vows are not to donald trump he  doesn't owe loyalty or fealty to a  political party or a certain president  um that was to me and to honor and  cherish and george and i have a lot of  things in common we've been married for  two decades we have four children  together another thing we have in common  is we both accepted very big jobs from  president trump yeah george took that  job started interviewing staff and then  changed his mind about president trump  he's welcome to do that but it was very  unlike george to be so publicly  bombastic he was always proud and how  did you handle that when you when you  went home i mean you write in the book  democracy will survive america will  survive not sure george conway and i  will survive it's very sad to me as we  sit here today did you all survive i'm  curious say it again as you sit here  today did you and did your marriage  survive well here we are i'm at the  shore this weekend with the kids lots of  kids they're with their friends but you  know yeah divorce people i'm going to go  but look you know sure i wish it was so  it's not someone like george to not take  action on something that means something  to him if it means that much to him i  think we should have gone to couples  counseling as ivanka trump put in her  post-it no and i think we all do what we  want with our time and i my objection is  that he spends his time doing that he's  welcome to do that but um look it's also  why wasn't i given the courtesy of being  told ahead of time tomorrow my op-ed  george george tell me my op-ed's going  to be in the new york times the  washington post i'm in the lincoln  project now we're going to have a new ad  yeah skewing your boss it was meant to  make me uncomfortable and let's face it  i quantify it in the book he was known  as kellyanne conway's husband  mostly described that way that's very  unusual i want to agree but but  curious knowing what you know now with  the sacrifices made within your own  family with with your with your kids  with your husband  you're not wearing a ring now as we as  we sit here he doesn't either would you  do it all again i would definitely serve  the country again and i think that the  trump pence administration had great  accomplishments for this country and  many measures energy independence the  economy that was humming even at the  beginning of the coronavirus cove and  getting those hundred thousand  ventilators making sure you want to work  for the president again ppe i would love  to work in the white house i would love  to serve at some level because white  house for the president president trump  well i would love to get rid of biden  and harris i think they've not done well  if you look at the polls you look at the  huge nbc news report today they're not  doing well i mean even are you and  george conway we're running out of time  kellyanne you're not going to talk to  your questions  well and thank you for reading this i  have many questions  it's a big book you said is it a  doorstop or a showstopper i think i  think it's both haley and conway thank  you very much here's the deal it's on  sale right now  give it a read it is worth your time

